# Python quality

- Target modern Python (3.12+) with type hints on public functions
- Keep modules small: routers / services / repositories separated
- Use explicit settings from environment variables; never hardcode secrets
- Prefer clear domain errors over bare exceptions
- Add migrations for every schema change
- No network calls inside request handlers without timeouts
- Format/lint with the repo-standard tools once introduced (ruff/mypy or equivalent)
- Do not add backend code during Phase 0 bootstrap
